\begin_layout Section
JTAG (IEEE 1149.1)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Joint Test Action Group (JTAG), formalized as the IEEE 1149.1 standard,
 provides a standardized serial boundary-scan architecture.
 It is primarily intended for structural testing, in-system programming,
 and embedded debugging of digital integrated circuits (ICs).
 JTAG has evolved into an indispensable interface, especially within modern
 System-on-Chip (SoC) and FPGA environments, enabling non-intrusive access
 to internal logic and registers.
 This capability facilitates design validation, post-silicon verification,
 board bring-up, and runtime diagnostics, making JTAG a cornerstone in contempor
ary digital design workflows.
\end_layout

