\begin_layout Subsection
JTAG Signal Description
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
TDI (Test Data In): 
\series default
\emph default
A unidirectional serial input line through which instruction or test data
 is injected into the target device.
 In multi-device configurations, it typically connects to the TDO of the
 preceding device.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
TDO (Test Data Out):
\series default
\emph default
 The serial output line that transmits the response data from the device.
 It is chained to the TDI of the subsequent device.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
TCK (Test Clock): 
\series default
\emph default
A dedicated clock signal for synchronizing all JTAG operations.
 It is independent of the system clock, enabling asynchronous test access.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
TMS (Test Mode Select): 
\series default
\emph default
Governs transitions within the TAP controller's state machine.
 The state of TMS is sampled on the rising edge of TCK.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
TRST (Test Reset – optional)
\series default
\emph default
: An asynchronous reset signal that forces the TAP controller into the Test-Logi
c-Reset state without requiring TCK activity.
\end_layout

